  "labelled_by": "Niccolò: applicability, dates and relations checked against the text; summaries drafted by Claude Code, not checked",
  "checked_by": "",
  "notes": "Applicability covers 172R, 172S, 182S, 182T, T182T, 206H, T206H: one row per range or single serial (25 rows); serial_from = serial_to for a single serial. The KAP 140 P/N list in (c)(1) splits '065-' / '00176-5201' across lines, so the condition's quote stops before the P/N list; the P/Ns in value are read from lines 248-250. The (e) table uses en dashes ('2003–24–13', '057–02203–0003') and one stray space ('2003– 24–13'); quotes keep them exactly, values use plain hyphens. The AD says 'KAP 140' in (c) and 'KC 140' (the computer unit) in (e). (c)(2) ‘certificated in any category’ is also required but narrows nothing, so it is not a condition."
}
